# Solar Power Forecasting and Inverter Fault Detection

A machine learning and deep learning project for **solar power prediction, plant-level forecasting, inverter fault detection, and anomaly detection** using photovoltaic plant generation and weather data.

## 📌 Project Overview

This project uses solar generation and weather sensor data from **two solar plants in India**. The workflow combines supervised learning, time-series forecasting, model transfer, and unsupervised anomaly detection.

### Main Objectives

* Predict inverter-level AC power from weather conditions.
* Identify under-performing inverters using prediction errors.
* Compare the worst inverter with the plant median.
* Forecast plant-level AC power one hour ahead.
* Compare LSTM forecasting with a persistence baseline.
* Test whether a Plant 1 model transfers to Plant 2.
* Detect inverter anomalies using an Autoencoder.

## 📊 Dataset

The dataset contains approximately **34 days of 15-minute interval data** from two solar plants.

Each plant contains:

* Generation data
* Weather sensor data
* Multiple inverter measurements

### Important Features

* `IRRADIATION`
* `MODULE_TEMPERATURE`
* `AMBIENT_TEMPERATURE`
* `AC_POWER`
* `DC_POWER`
* `SOURCE_KEY`
* `DATE_TIME`

## 🔧 Technologies Used

* Python
* Pandas
* NumPy
* Matplotlib
* Scikit-learn
* TensorFlow / Keras
* Google Colab

## 🤖 Model A — MLP AC Power Prediction

A Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) regression model predicts inverter AC power using:

* Irradiation
* Module temperature
* Ambient temperature
* Hour of day

Night-time observations were excluded from the Model A analysis because zero-generation rows dominate the dataset.

### Plant 1 Results

| Metric |  Result |
| ------ | ------: |
| MAE    | 26.2533 |
| R²     |  0.9831 |

## ⚠️ Inverter Fault Detection

The difference between actual and predicted AC power was used to identify under-performing inverters.

### Worst-Performing Inverter

```text
bvBOhCH3iADSZry
```

Its results were:

| Metric              |    Value |
| ------------------- | -------: |
| Mean Error          | -34.9204 |
| Mean Absolute Error |  40.0287 |

A negative mean error indicates that the inverter generally produced less power than the model expected.

## 📉 Worst Inverter vs Plant Median

The worst-performing inverter was compared with the median AC power of all inverters at each timestamp.

```text
Worst inverter mean AC power: 526.9991
Plant median mean AC power:   572.4267
Mean difference:              -45.4276
```

This indicates that the selected inverter generated approximately **45.43 AC-power units less than the plant median on average**.

## 🔮 Model B — 1-Hour Plant Forecast

An LSTM model was used to forecast the next **4 × 15-minute steps**, representing one hour of plant-level AC power.

The model used the previous **16 time steps (4 hours)** along with weather and plant power information.

### LSTM vs Persistence

| Model       |    MAE |
| ----------- | -----: |
| LSTM        | 0.0559 |
| Persistence | 0.0622 |

The **LSTM performed better than the persistence baseline**.

## 🔄 Plant 2 Transfer

The MLP trained on Plant 1 was applied to Plant 2 **without retraining** to evaluate whether the learned relationship transferred between plants.

This provides a simple test of model transferability across solar plants.

## 🧠 Autoencoder Anomaly Detection

As a stretch goal, an Autoencoder was trained using:

* Irradiation
* Module temperature
* Ambient temperature
* AC power

The reconstruction error was used as an anomaly score.

### Highest Anomaly Scores

The highest reconstruction error was observed for:

```text
1BY6WEcLGh8j5v7
```

The previously identified under-performing inverter:

```text
bvBOhCH3iADSZry
```

was also ranked among the highest anomaly scores, providing additional evidence of unusual behaviour.

## 📈 Project Workflow

```text
Solar Generation + Weather Data
              ↓
       Data Preprocessing
              ↓
      Daylight Filtering
              ↓
       Exploratory Analysis
              ↓
     ┌────────┴─────────┐
     ↓                  ↓
   MLP Model          LSTM Model
     ↓                  ↓
AC Power Prediction   1-Hour Forecast
     ↓                  ↓
Fault Detection      Persistence
     ↓                  ↓
Inverter Ranking     Comparison
     ↓
Plant Median Analysis

              +
              
        Autoencoder
              ↓
      Reconstruction Error
              ↓
       Anomaly Ranking
```

