## 🎯 Key Takeaways

* The MLP achieved strong performance for inverter-level AC power prediction.
* Prediction errors can be used to identify potentially under-performing inverters.
* The worst inverter produced substantially less power than the plant median.
* The LSTM outperformed the persistence baseline for one-hour forecasting.
* A Plant 1-trained model can be tested for transferability to Plant 2 without retraining.
* Autoencoder reconstruction error provides an additional method for inverter anomaly detection.

